Subject: [PATCH] perf unwind: Use available map release helpers in libdw unwinder

Linux 6.6.133 calls map_symbol__exit() when releasing libdw unwind entries,
but this branch has no definition of that helper. This causes perf to
fail to link when libdw unwinding is enabled.

Release the map and maps references directly using the helpers available
in 6.6, balancing the references acquired in entry(). The entries are
freed immediately afterwards, so their fields do not need to be cleared.

--- a/tools/perf/util/unwind-libdw.c
+++ b/tools/perf/util/unwind-libdw.c
@@ -319,8 +319,10 @@ int unwind__get_entries(unwind_entry_cb_t
 	if (err)
 		pr_debug("unwind: failed with '%s'\n", dwfl_errmsg(-1));
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ui->idx; i++)
-		map_symbol__exit(&ui->entries[i].ms);
+	for (i = 0; i < ui->idx; i++) {
+		map__put(ui->entries[i].ms.map);
+		maps__put(ui->entries[i].ms.maps);
+	}
 
 	dwfl_end(ui->dwfl);
 	free(ui);
